.\" fansctl.1 - manual page for fansctl
.\" AGPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/askender/fansctl
.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt FANSCTL 1
.Os macOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm fansctl
.Nd fan control and power survey for Apple Silicon Macs \(em one binary, menu bar app + CLI
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm subcommand
.Op Ar arguments
.\" ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a single dependency-free binary (C / AppKit, no Electron) that talks to the
SMC through the 80-byte Apple Silicon ABI.
.Pp
Started with no arguments it becomes a menu bar app (it forks to the
background and does not occupy the terminal).
With a subcommand it acts as a CLI.
The CLI follows the system language
.Pq Ev FANSCTL_LANG , LC_ALL , LC_MESSAGES , LANG ;
daemon logs
.Pq smart/hold
always stay in Chinese so they remain greppable.
.Ss COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "bar uninstall"
.It Ic fans
Fan RPMs, minimum and maximum (read-only).
.It Ic status
Current/target RPMs and mode per fan (read-only).
.It Ic temps Op Fl -sort Op Fl -above Ar N
All temperature sensors (read-only), with human-readable names where known
.Pq SoC, CPU P/E-cores, GPU, memory, NAND, battery, airflow...
and the raw SMC key.
.Fl -sort
orders hottest first;
.Fl -above
filters by a °C floor.
.It Ic power
Power survey (read-only): system draw
.Pq SMC key PSTR ,
power-input telemetry, adapter rating, battery, USB devices' declared current
draw, and top power processes.
.It Ic power Fl -watch Op Ar seconds
Continuous power monitoring (default 5 s); with
.Fl -json
emits one JSON object per line for logging pipelines.
.It Ic dump
Dump every SMC key with decoded values.
.It Ic watch Op Ar seconds
Refresh loop, default 2 s.
.It Ic set Ar rpm Op Ar fan
Set RPM (clamped to the safe range); without a fan index, all fans.
.It Ic max Op Ar fan
Full speed.
.It Ic auto Op Ar fan
Restore system auto control.
.It Ic smart Op Ar low high
Smart curve daemon: below
.Ar low
fans follow the system, above
.Ar high
full speed, linear in between (default 40~80\(*C).
.It Im smart stop
Stop the smart daemon (including instances started from the menu bar) and
restore auto.
.It Ic hold Ar target
Thermostat daemon: a PI closed loop holds the hottest sensor at
.Ar target
(default 70\(*C); mutually exclusive with
.Ic smart .
.It Ic hold stop
Stop the thermostat and restore auto.
.It Ic bar install
Install the menu bar auto-start LaunchAgent
.Pq Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.fansctl.bar.plist ,
pointing at the current executable; no sudo needed.
.It Ic bar uninstall
Remove the LaunchAgent and stop the menu bar app.
.It Ic bar status
Show whether auto-start is installed, loaded, and the menu bar is running.
.It Ic doctor
Collect diagnostics (model, SMC keys, fans, sensors, helper, LaunchAgent,
daemons, battery) for issue reports.
.It Ic version
Print the version.
.El
.Pp
Commands that change fan state
.Pq Ic set , max , auto , smart , hold
need root
.Pq Xr sudo 8 .
.Ss NOTIFICATIONS
.Ic smart
sends a system notification once when the temperature reaches the high
threshold (fans at full speed); the thermostat
.Pq Ic hold
notifies when it cannot hold the target (more than 3\((*C above it, fans
already at full speed). The alert re-arms after the temperature drops back.
Both use a Notification Center banner via
.Xr osascript 1 ;
the first one may ask for notification permission.
.Ss JSON OUTPUT
The read commands
.Ic fans , status , temps , power , watch
accept
.Fl -json
and emit machine-readable JSON (keys in English regardless of interface
language; unknown values are
.Li null ) .
Temperature entries carry a
.Li name
field (English, null when unknown).
.Ic watch --json
and
.Ic power --json --watch
print one complete JSON object per line (JSON Lines), suitable for piping
into
.Xr jq 1
or a monitoring pipeline.
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fansctl status --json
fansctl watch --json 5 | jq -c '.fans[0].actual_rpm'
fansctl power --json --watch 5 | jq -c '.system_w'
fansctl temps --json | jq -r '.temps[].celsius' | sort -n | tail -1
.Ed
.Ss PRIVILEGES
A setuid-root helper copy
.Pq Pa /usr/local/bin/fansctl-root ,
installed with
.Cm make install-root ,
lets the menu bar control fans without password prompts.
In the helper context only fixed fan verbs
.Pq Ic __apply , __smart , __hold , smart stop )
are allowed; it is never a generic privileged execution entry point.
A system LaunchDaemon
.Pq Cm make install-restore
restores auto mode at boot as a safety net.
.Ss ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "FANSCTL_LANG"
.It Ev FANSCTL_LANG
Override the CLI language
.Pq Cm zh / Cm en ;
takes precedence over the locale variables.
.It Ev FANSCTL_DEBUG
Print SMC protocol details to stderr.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/bin/fansctl-root"
.It Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.fansctl.bar.plist
Menu bar auto-start (managed by
.Ic bar install/uninstall ).
.It Pa /tmp/fansctl.bar.log
Menu bar log.
.It Pa /tmp/fansctl.smart.pid , /tmp/fansctl.hold.pid , /tmp/fansctl.bar.pid
Daemon/instance state files shared between CLI and menu bar.
.It Pa /tmp/fansctl.smart.log , /tmp/fansctl.hold.log
Daemon logs (Chinese by design).
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/fansctl-root
Setuid helper (optional).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 on success, non-zero on errors such as missing SMC, permission
denied, or invalid arguments.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fansctl status                 # read-only overview
sudo fansctl smart 55 85       # smart curve, 55~85\(*C
sudo fansctl set 3000          # all fans to 3000 rpm
sudo fansctl max && sleep 10 && sudo fansctl auto
fansctl power                  # who is eating the watts
fansctl bar install            # menu bar starts at login
fansctl doctor                 # attach to issue reports
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
Project README (bilingual:
.Pa README.md
and
.Pa README.zh-CN.md )
at
.Lk https://github.com/askender/fansctl .
